\b RBAC Implementation Notes - Card Management System\b0\par
\par
\b 1) Objective\b0\par
Implement dynamic role-based access control (RBAC) where:\par
- Menus are driven from backend API, not hardcoded only.\par
- Roles are managed from admin UI.\par
- Role-to-menu and user-to-role assignment are configurable.\par
- Frontend route access follows assigned menus.\par
- Backend enforces authorization on management APIs.\par
\par
\b 2) What Was Implemented\b0\par
\b Backend\b0\par
- Added/extended menu APIs:\par
  - GET /api/my-menus\par
  - GET /api/menus\par
  - POST /api/menus\par
  - PUT /api/menus/{id}\par
  - DELETE /api/menus/{id}\par
- Added role-menu assignment APIs:\par
  - GET /api/roles/{roleCode}/menus\par
  - POST /api/roles/{roleCode}/menus\par
  - DELETE /api/roles/{roleCode}/menus/{menuId}\par
- Added user-role assignment APIs:\par
  - GET /api/users/{id}/roles\par
  - POST /api/users/{id}/roles\par
  - DELETE /api/users/{id}/roles/{roleCode}\par
- Login/refresh now include menus in auth response.\par
- Added method-level authorization for management endpoints (ADMIN/SECURITY_MANAGER/SUPER_ADMIN).\par
- Added migration V24 to seed additional menus.\par
- Added migration V25 to grant all menus to ADMIN.\par
\par
\b Frontend\b0\par
- Added menu types and service integration with backend APIs.\par
- Added RBAC utility for menu storage/access checks.\par
- Auth context now stores menus from login/refresh.\par
- Sidebar now renders dynamic menus from backend response.\par
- Route guard checks hasMenuAccess(path) and redirects to /unauthorized when blocked.\par
- Added Unauthorized page.\par
- Added Menu Management screen (security/menus).\par
- Extended Role screen with menu assignment dialog.\par
\par
\b 3) Core Data Model Used\b0\par
- USM_USER: users\par
- USM_GROUP: roles\par
- USM_USER_GROUP: user-role mapping\par
- CMS_MENU: menu master\par
- CMS_ROLE_MENU: role-menu mapping\par
\par
\b 4) End-to-End Runtime Flow\b0\par
1. User logs in.\par
2. Backend authenticates and fetches user roles.\par
3. JWT is generated with role claims.\par
4. Backend fetches menus for those roles.\par
5. Frontend stores token and menus.\par
6. Sidebar is built from allowed menus.\par
7. Route guard allows/block routes by menu path.\par
8. Backend still enforces role checks for protected APIs.\par
\par
\b 5) Key Fixes Done During Implementation\b0\par
- Fixed date filter issue in card search (LocalDate handling).\par
- Added expiry screen actions:\par
  - Renew card (expiry +5 years from card expiry month).\par
  - Replace card (replacement request flow).\par
- Fixed replacement generation path to update the replacement-target card and PAN-linked records.\par
- Fixed role resolution edge cases:\par
  - Support role retrieval robustness.\par
  - Added compatibility for login/user role lookup behavior.\par
- Fixed admin menu access by seeding/granting complete mappings.\par
\par
\b 6) Testing Checklist (Functional)\b0\par
\b A. Admin baseline\b0\par
- Login as admin.\par
- Confirm roles in login response include ADMIN.\par
- Confirm menus list is returned.\par
- Open security/users, security/roles, security/menus.\par
\par
\b B. Create and assign restricted role\b0\par
- Create role CARD_TESTER.\par
- Assign only selected menus.\par
- Create test user and assign CARD_TESTER.\par
- Login as test user and verify limited sidebar.\par
- Try blocked route directly and verify redirect to /unauthorized.\par
\par
\b C. Backend protection\b0\par
- With restricted user token, call admin endpoints.\par
- Expected result: 403 Forbidden.\par
\par
\b D. Dynamic update check\b0\par
- Add/remove menu from a role.\par
- Re-login test user.\par
- Verify sidebar changes without redeployment.\par
\par
\b 7) DB Verification Queries\b0\par
1) User-role mapping:\par
SELECT LOGIN_ID, GROUP_ID FROM USM_USER_GROUP WHERE UPPER(LOGIN_ID) IN ('ADMIN','RBAC_USER');\par
\par
2) Role-menu mapping:\par
SELECT ROLE_CODE, MENU_ID FROM CMS_ROLE_MENU WHERE ROLE_CODE IN ('ADMIN','CARD_TESTER') ORDER BY ROLE_CODE, MENU_ID;\par
\par
3) Menu master:\par
SELECT ID, MENU_NAME, MENU_PATH, STATUS FROM CMS_MENU ORDER BY SORT_ORDER, ID;\par
\par
\b 8) Lessons Learned / Notes\b0\par
- Dynamic RBAC is best when UI access and backend auth are both enforced.\par
- Frontend checks improve UX but are not security boundaries.\par
- Keep role codes consistent across user-role and role-menu mappings.\par
- After role/menu updates, users should re-login or refresh auth payload.\par
- Prefer idempotent DB migrations for menu seed and grants.\par
\par
\b 9) Next Improvements (Recommended)\b0\par
- Add fine-grained permission checks per business API (not just admin APIs).\par
- Add audit logging for role/menu assignment changes.\par
- Add cache invalidation strategy for role/menu updates.\par
- Add super-admin policy model explicitly (if needed).\par
